WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.857
Step 1. Open the activity definitions.

1.2
00:00:02.857 --> 00:00:08.415
An activity definition is a template that clinicians use to order a service for a

1.3
00:00:08.415 --> 00:00:13.924
patient. In Settings, in the Clinical group, select Activity Definitions.

2.1
00:00:13.924 --> 00:00:19.377
Step 2. Open a category. Select the category for the new activity definition,

2.2
00:00:19.377 --> 00:00:25.282
and keep opening subcategories until you reach a category with no subcategories.

3.1
00:00:25.282 --> 00:00:30.219
Step 3. Start the activity definition. Select Add Activity Definition.

3.2
00:00:30.219 --> 00:00:35.575
Care opens the Create Activity Definition form and sets Resource Category to the

3.3
00:00:35.575 --> 00:00:37.749
category that you opened.

4.1
00:00:37.749 --> 00:00:40.667
Step 4. Fill in the basic information.

4.2
00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:44.529
Enter the Title, Description, Usage, Category and Code.

4.3
00:00:44.529 --> 00:01:10.047
Category is the type of service, and Resource Category is the folder that holds it.

5.1
00:01:10.047 --> 00:01:13.911
Step 8. Save the activity definition. Select Create.

5.2
00:01:13.911 --> 00:01:17.526
Care shows Activity definition created successfully.

5.3
00:01:17.526 --> 00:01:24.916
If its status is Active, clinicians can pick it when they order a service.
